    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0865" n="833" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10/pg833"/>

                <head>348. Memorandum From the Assistant Secretary of State for Inter-American
                    Affairs (Martin) to the Deputy Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs
                        (Johnson)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d348-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-06-27">June 27,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Priorities Schedule for Cuba</item>
                </list>
                <p>There is attached for your information the list of the Departmentʼs courses of
                    action with regard to Cuba which I had shown to you and was subsequently
                    provided General Lansdale.</p>
                <p>General Lansdale indicated that he thought this was a good start, although he
                    was, of course, disappointed that the list contained no dramatic event that
                    could be accomplished before the review.</p>


                <xi:include href="d348-a1.xml" xpointer="d348-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
